--- a function taking a function is one function for every call (spec,
--- Specialization): two calls handing it functions that answer two kinds
--- are refused, naming both — the parameter had been typed by one, and
--- the call handing the other did not build compiled, while the
--- interpreter ran both (Rosetta Code, Monads/List monad)

fn applied[x, f]
    return f[x]

fn twice[x]
    return x * 2

fn shown[x]
    return '<`x`>'

log[applied[3, twice]]
log[applied[3, shown]]
